`create_content()` (used by `@pytest.mark.portal(content=...)`) reindexed each item individually, which only enqueues work in `Products.CMFCore.indexing`'s per-thread queue rather than applying it. A direct index read such as `uniqueValuesFor()` bypasses the flush that `CatalogTool.searchResults()` and friends perform on their own, so it saw whatever had already reached the index and nothing more, typically missing the item created last. The fixture now calls `processQueue()` once after creating all content, so index reads see everything the marker created. @afonsojanu
